                                                    "text": "you can change preset from outside by sending in the first inlet the preset number (int or float) with a prepend \"preset\" "
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                                    "linecount": 18,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 11.0, 64.0, 393.0, 248.0 ],
                                                    "text": "snippet for jit.gl.camera\n\na virtual 3d camera, a view into your 3d scene\n\nyou can position it and rotate it to make it look whereever\n\nif locklook is ON, you do not control the rotation but give X Y Z of where the camera should look at, meaning that if you feed the lookat X Y Z with the coordinates of a moving object, the camera will follow it\n\ntripod ON will stabilize your camera like its on a tripod\n\nthe viewport makes it so that the camera renders only in a quadrant of the world / window output, so you can use a multicam set up for the same output window\n\nnear and far clip is the distance range from the camera to actually render, any geometry outside this range will not be visible"
                                                }
                                            },
